    "critique": "This backtest shows a strategy that loses money in both training and validation, with mean returns of -34.6% and -18.4% respectively, and the loss is worse than the no-condition baseline (-8.4%/-5.2%). The validation sample is very small (34 trades, 12 blocks), and its confidence interval still includes zero, so there is no reliable evidence of an edge. The apparent improvement from train to validation is likely noise rather than robustness, and the condition merely selects a subset of even worse trades. Stricter cost assumptions push the validation lower bound to -42%, reinforcing that the realistic outcome is strongly negative. The single worst trade lost nearly 100%, and the worst 10-day window lost 631%, indicating extreme tail risk.",
